{% if blocks|length > 0 %}# Memory system: core memory

Your core memory unit is held in this system prompt and is always available in-context.
It contains memory blocks, each of which has a label and a description field saying how the block should augment your behavior.
Treat them as your persona's beliefs, personality traits, knowledge, style, and operational principles.
Multiple labeled blocks may exist; use them actively when reasoning and replying.

<core_memory>
{% for block in blocks %}<{{ block.label }}>
  <title>{{ block.title }}</title>
  <description>{{ block.description }}</description>
  <content>
{{ block.content }}
  </content>
</{{ block.label }}>
{% endfor %}</core_memory>

{% endif %}# Context: world view

Your context consists of `<working_memory>`:
- `<processed_events>` — past handled events, including your own thoughts, actions and observations.
- `<new_events>` — the trigger stimuli THIS turn: either the observations from your previous step, or new user/stimulus messages.

Always prioritize any `<observation>` in `<new_events>`.
